# Incident Categorisation - Migration Map

**v0.2 (2026-07-08).** Every current LIMSOC incident type mapped to its new home in the proposed model (see Model Design). Source: `IncidentTypes-2026-07-08.xlsx` (72 types, exported from LIMSOC 2026-07-08). Rows marked **FLAG** need a decision before the map is final. Everything else follows mechanically from the locked rules.

Legend for the New Home column. `Type:` a node in the new tree. `Tag:` a controlled tag. `Outcome:` an Incident Outcome value. `Status:` carried by Agency Status. `Out:` leaves the incident taxonomy.

## SAR (4 types)

| Code | Current type | New home | Notes |
|------|--------------|----------|-------|
| A01 | Missing Person - Land | Type: SAR > Search > Person, Tag: Land | Land/water becomes a Tag. Tree has one Person node |
| A02 | Missing Person - Water | Type: SAR > Search > Person, Tag: Water | As above |
| A03 | Missing Vessel | Type: SAR > Search > Vessel | Direct |
| A04 | AMSA Tasking | **FLAG** Type: External Agency > Tasking, Tag: AMSA | Whose-incident rule says Tasking (AMSA's job, we are a resource). But these are SAR jobs and moving them out of the SAR family changes SAR statistics. Confirm the stats treatment before locking |

